  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as <strong>Assertion A</strong> and the other is labelled as <strong>Reason R</strong>.</p><p><strong>Assertion A</strong>: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>of hydrated oxalic acid dissolved in water to make <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></math> solution will result in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>M</mi></math> oxalic acid solution.</p><p><strong>Reason R</strong>: Molar mass of hydrated oxalic acid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>126</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>o</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> .</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XtvYB",
      "text": "Both <strong>A</strong> and <strong>R</strong> are true but <strong>R</strong> is <strong>NOT</strong> the correct explanation of <strong>A</strong>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nsGx5",
      "text": "<strong>A</strong> is true but <strong>R</strong> is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1bbPo",
      "text": "Both <strong>A</strong> and <strong>R</strong> are true and <strong>R</strong> is the correct explanation of <strong>A</strong>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gK8Ej",
      "text": "<strong>A</strong> is false but <strong>R</strong> is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Molarity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>wt</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>mwt</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1000</mn></math></p><p>Using this formula, we can calculate the molarity of the oxalic acid solution as follows:</p><ol>\t<li>Mass of hydrated oxalic acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></li>\t<li>Molar mass of hydrated oxalic acid<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>)</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>126</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>064</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></li>\t<li>Volume of the solution = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math></li></ol><p>Molarity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>126</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>250</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>So both assertion land reason are correct.</p>",
